Z||000000||loren||02-05-2001||09:32 AM||||i have a serious oil leak coming from around the timing cover shaft seal on my 85 gt 6 cyl.<BR>how do i determine if it is a front main seal or just a timing cover seal leaking ?<P>i sure would appreciate some info.<BR>loren||||reg||1
Z||000001||2birds||02-05-2001||09:45 PM||||The seal is pretty easy to replace, just like the axle seals in your transaxle case.  Just be careful not to damage it while inserting it.<BR>The balancer usually gets grooves worn in the cast iron surfce by the front cover seal, though.  A stainless steel sleeve kit is available for the balancer from Fel-Pro (got mine from Advance Auto for around $8).  Really easy to put on, just clean the balancer shaft with some 400 grit wet-or-dry sandpaper before installing.  The only PITA tool was the balancer puller, which some stores will loan out (Autozone comes to mind).  <BR>While you're into it, you may want to replace the timing chain and gears, depending on mileage.  Not too much more work, since you have to put it up in the air and remove the RR wheel and inner fender liner to get the balancer off anyway.  <BR>In for a penny, in for a pound (or two).<P>Anyway, sleeving the balancer and putting in a new seal finally fixed my oil leaks (AND belt squeal).||||reg||1
